Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Sure!  You can write an “if-then” program as such:

```C
#include <stdio.h>

int main()
{
    int x;
    scanf("%d", &x);

    if(x <= 10)
    {
        //do something
    }
    else
    {
        //do something else
    }

    return 0;
}
```

This example code reads an integer from the standard input stream, stores it in the variable x, and then checks whether the value of x is less than or equal to 10. In this case, the program does nothing, so the else branch is not executed, but you can put code in the else branch if you want.
